    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f0d7e1c9",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: once_you_go_black_ur_a_single_mom; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a white woman holding a Black child, with text stating 'once you go black ur a single mom!' This frames Black identity as inherently linked to single motherhood, which is a harmful stereotype rooted in racialized assumptions about Black families. It implies that being Black is synonymous with being a single parent, which is a false and demeaning generalization. This trope is part of a broader pattern of 'welfare dependency' and 'single motherhood' stereotypes used to pathologize and dehumanize Black communities. The intent is to perpetuate a racist narrative that equates Blackness with economic hardship and familial instability, thereby reinforcing systemic prejudice. The juxtaposition of the image (a smiling, seemingly affluent white woman with a Black child) with the text creates a false equivalence and reinforces the harmful stereotype that Black children are only found in single-mother households, which is both inaccurate and demeaning. This meme is hateful because it targets Black people based on their race and perpetuates a harmful, racist stereotype that devalues Black families and implies that Black children are only found in single-mother households, which is a false and demeaning generalization.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_69990505"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
